&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Advanced Digital Technology (ADT) Crash Safety group builds Scout’s physics-AI crash digital twins, integrating full-vehicle CAE, subsystem models, and physical test data to enable early, high-accuracy safety predictions. The team plays a critical role in guiding structural, restraint, and occupant-safety decisions long before prototypes exist, directly influencing program safety ratings and sign-off readiness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This internship will support the team by executing hands-on crash simulation tasks, validating digital models against sled and crash-test data, and helping streamline our test–simulation correlation workflows. The intern will contribute to the architecture of the crash digital twin, improving predictive capability and accelerating safety decision-making for Scout programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Daily Responsibilities of the Internship Program include&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
