&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The purpose of the Human Resources Summer Internship is to provide students with hands-on, real-world experience in Human Resources while supporting the day-to-day operations and strategic initiatives of the HR team. This internship is designed to develop foundational HR skills, expose interns to core HR functions—including onboarding, employee engagement, workforce development, and community outreach—and offer meaningful project-based learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through this experience, interns will gain insight into how HR supports employees, leaders, and the organization while building professional skills, industry knowledge, and confidence for a future career in Human Resources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Daily Responsibilities of the Internship Program include&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with day-to-day HR operations and general administrative tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide administrative support to the HR team, including document preparation and data organization
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new hire onboarding for direct and indirect employees, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing welcome packets and orientation materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completing onboarding checklists and coordination tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and design a 90-Day Performance Review process and materials for hourly employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support K-12 volunteer and community engagement projects, including planning and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
