&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Astranis builds advanced satellites for high orbits, expanding humanity’s reach into the solar system. Today, Astranis satellites provide dedicated, secure networks to highly-sophisticated customers across the globe— large enterprises, sovereign governments, and the US military. With five satellites on orbit and many more set to launch soon, the company is servicing a backlog of more than $1 billion of commercial contracts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Astranis is the preferred satellite communications partner for buyers with stringent requirements for uptime, data security, network visibility, and customization. Astranis has raised over $750 million from some of the world’s best investors, from Andreessen Horowitz to Blackrock and Fidelity, and employs a team of 450 engineers and entrepreneurs. Astranis designs, builds, and operates its satellites out of its 153,000 sq. ft. headquarters in Northern California, USA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vulnerability Management Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astranis is looking for a Vulnerability Management Analyst who is ready to proactively identify and neutralize threats before they materialize. Our ideal candidate is passionate about security and has a talent for discovering vulnerabilities, assessing risk, and orchestrating remediation across a diverse technological landscape. With the threat landscape constantly shifting, we need a sharp, detail-oriented individual who can stay ahead of potential exploits, safeguard our systems, and ensure the resilience and integrity of our digital infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle all vulnerability scans across the enterprise, including identifying application and configuration vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, manage, and track patching and remediation plans in collaboration with system owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and validate system patching and configuration fixes across Windows, macOS, and Linux operating systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the risk of and prioritize vulnerabilities based on their criticality, system exposure, and potential business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and maintain the vulnerability management platform (Tenable) to ensure effective scanning and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze scan results, create detailed reports on the vulnerability landscape, and communicate findings to technical teams and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in developing and maturing the overall vulnerability management program and associated policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with emerging threats, vulnerabilities, and security technologies to continuously improve our security posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in a security-related role, with a strong background in security principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in cybersecurity, specifically in vulnerability management, risk assessment, and patch management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with vulnerability management tools, especially Tenable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how to assess risk and determine the criticality of security vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with patching and security configuration for Windows, macOS, and Linux environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of security standards, system hardening principles, and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience with security vulnerability scanners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-tech, or aerospace environment.&lt;/li&gt;
