&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of&amp;nbsp;enabling human life on Mars.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SPACEPORT ENGINEER (STARSHIP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starbase is the center of SpaceX&#39;s plans to revolutionize space travel, serving as our primary site for Starship development and operations. We&#39;re seeking a licensed Professional Engineer to serve as our internal &quot;City Engineer.&quot; &amp;nbsp;This individual will ensure that all civil engineering projects at Starbase meet the highest standards of quality, compliance, and innovation. In this role, you&#39;ll own the permitting process for infrastructure developments, bridging the gap between our internal teams, consultants, and local authorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary owner and reviewer for final plan documents produced by internal engineering teams and external consultants, ensuring they are submission ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop standardized form plan sets, establish minimum standards, and create checklists to guide engineers in producing high-quality, compliant engineering documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert guidance to cross-functional teams on the status of plans, including readiness assessments for stamping and submission, to streamline workflows and minimize delays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with project managers, designers, and stakeholders to resolve technical issues, optimize designs for efficiency, and incorporate innovative solutions that align with SpaceX&#39;s rapid iteration ethos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date on the latest in civil engineering codes, permitting processes, and best practices to ensure Starbase&#39;s infrastructure supports our aggressive launch and development timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the continuous improvement of our engineering documentation processes, fostering a culture of excellence and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of working with municipal or local authorities on infrastructure projects, including document submission and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in an engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Licensed Professional Engineer (P.E.) in the state of Texas, with the ability to stamp and certify plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in civil engineering, including project management, plan development, and permitting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-stakes, fast-paced environments such as aerospace, construction, or large-scale industrial developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Texas-specific regulations, including those relevant to coastal or high-growth areas like Starbase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills to mentor engineers and provide clear, actionable feedback on plan development stages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in engineering software tools (e.g., GIS, AutoCAD, Civil 3D) and document management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in ambiguous situations, adapting quickly to evolving project needs while maintaining rigorous standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for space exploration and a willingness to relocate to work in Starbase, Texas, to be at the forefront of humanity&#39;s multiplanetary future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills to mentor engineers and provide clear, actionable feedback on plan development stages.&lt;/li&gt;
